# Which AstraPlugins commit states the manifest rules this bot enforces.
#
# THIS FILE IS THE ONLY PLACE THE PIN IS WRITTEN. Registry plan B-T1.4.
#
# It lived in `.github/workflows/ingest.yml`'s workflow-level `env:` and three
# readers grepped it out of there with `grep -oP '^\s*ASTRA_PLUGINS_REF:\s*\K…'`.
# Two things were wrong with that and only one of them is cosmetic:
#
#   * B-T5.2 DELETES `ingest.yml` at R6. A pin that lives inside a file with a
#     deletion date is a pin whose readers all break on the day it is deleted,
#     and they break by finding nothing — `grep || true` yields the empty
#     string, and only `bot-tests.yml` and `build-index.yml` turn that into an
#     error. `tools/coverage/reserved-id-mirror.mjs` reads it for a URL and had
#     no such guard.
#   * Between R1 and R4b the pin is BUMPED (AP-7's registry readers; M-T5.7).
#     Every bump was a diff inside a 1300-line workflow, where the reviewer
#     reads YAML and the change is a fact about another repository.
#
# Shape: `KEY=VALUE`, one per line, `#` comments. Not YAML and not JSON, so a
# shell can `source` it, a workflow can append it to `$GITHUB_ENV` unchanged,
# and `link-deps.sh` — which already refuses to clone without
# `ASTRA_PLUGINS_REF` — needs no parser.
#
# `sign.yml` does not read this file and must not: no signing job reads another
# repository (registry plan seam 4). `bot/tests/workflows.test.mjs` asserts it.
#
# AFTER R3 EXITS, MOVING THE SHA BELOW NEEDS AN OPERATOR ACKNOWLEDGEMENT. This
# file is in TRUST-31's hashed set, and that is the right price: the pin selects
# the manifest rules a stranger's listing is judged by.
#
# ── the history, moved here verbatim from ingest.yml ────────────────────────
env:
# The AstraPlugins commit whose `astra-plugin-manifest` this bot validates
# manifests with. Pinned by SHA, never by branch: the crate is the daemon's
# own parser, and "whatever HEAD says today" is not a thing to decide a
# stranger's listing with. Bump it deliberately, in a reviewed commit.
#
# The note that used to be here said this SHA was the tip of an unpushed
# branch, and that a pin nobody can fetch "fails loudly, which is the right
# failure". Both halves stopped being true. That branch was rewritten before it
# was pushed, so the commit is on no reachable ref and never will be —
# `fatal: unable to read tree (50eaa616…)` — and the failure was not loud at
# all: `selftest` failed, `check` was skipped, and the first real submission
# got "the ingest job did not produce a report", which reads as a fault
# somewhere in the bot rather than as a one-line pin.
#
# It was for a while the same commit as `plugin-release/v1` and as the one
# `trust.json` allows an attestation from. **They have now diverged, and that
# is correct.** This pin says which manifest rules a listing is judged by, and
# moving it is a code review. `trust.json`'s allowlist says which builder's
# word is worth anything, and moving that is a root-key ceremony. Tying a
# cheap decision to an expensive one means either the cheap one stops moving
# or the expensive one gets made casually.
#
# Bumped to `aaf480ea` for `spec/icon-formats.yaml`, which the icon-format
# coupling in `tools/validate.mjs` reads. Safe to move: `astra-plugin-manifest`
# and `plugin-release.yml` are byte-identical between the two commits
# (`git diff --stat e3329df2 aaf480ea -- <path>` is empty for both), so no
# manifest is judged differently and no attestation changes meaning.
#
# Bumped to `6d6861f` for `spec/locales.yaml`, `spec/listing-limits.yaml` and
# `testdata/locales/`, which the three locale couplings in `tools/validate.mjs`
# read. This one is NOT byte-identical, and the check is the same one, run
# again rather than repeated from memory:
#
#   * `astra-plugin-cli/vendor/astra-plugin-manifest` gains a `Cargo.lock` and
#     one named constant — `NOARCH_PLATFORM_KEY = "noarch"`, replacing the
#     literal in `RESERVED_PLATFORM_KEYS` and re-exported from `lib.rs`. No
#     parse, no rule, no field changes, so no manifest is judged differently.
#     (`git diff aaf480ea 6d6861f -- astra-plugin-cli/vendor/astra-plugin-manifest/src`.)
#   * `plugin-release.yml` moves its own `ASTRA_TOOLING_REF` to the CLI that
#     knows about `locales/`. That is a change to what an AUTHOR's release
#     builds with, and it reaches this registry through the bundle, not
#     through this pin. Which builder's word counts is the
#     `reusable_workflow_shas` allowlist inside the root-signed `trust.json`
#     — its own list of commits, which this variable does not appear in and
#     cannot move — so no attestation changes meaning here either.
#
# Bumped to `c545528` for the three locale caps `spec/listing-limits.yaml`
# gained. `checkMirroredListingLimits` in `tools/validate.mjs` enumerates this
# repository's `<cap>_mirrored_by` declarations and asks whether the copy each
# names exists over there — so with the pin at `6d6861f` that check reported
# three real errors about a file that had since grown the rows, which is the
# correct verdict about the pinned commit and the wrong one about AstraPlugins.
# Measured, both ways:
#
#   $ ASTRA_PLUGINS_DIR=<AstraPlugins@6d6861f> node tools/validate.mjs --allow-staging
#   ERROR ... max_locale_bytes is declared `_mirrored_by` this file, which has no
#         `max_locale_bytes` row                                    (x3)  FAIL
#   $ ASTRA_PLUGINS_DIR=<AstraPlugins@c545528> node tools/validate.mjs --allow-staging
#   PASS  15 plugin(s), 0 error(s)
#
# This is the C16 discipline again — that checkout moved in its own commit
# BEFORE anything read it — applied to a comparison rather than to a corpus.
#
# Bumped again to `2d35d2d`, and THIS bump is not optional in the way the
# others were. `CORPUS_RULE_IDS` in bot/lib/locales.mjs now maps
# `E_LOCALE_CARD_TOO_LARGE` to the corpus id `E19`, and the reader below holds
# every mapped rule to having a fail case upstream. That case —
# `testdata/locales/fail/card-i18n-over-budget` — exists only from `2d35d2d`.
# Map without pin is an immediate red: `rule E19 is implemented here and has
# no fail case in the corpus`. So the two land together, and this comment is
# the reason they cannot be separated later by somebody tidying.
#
# That pairing is also what broke a cycle. The fixture could not go upstream
# first — a case expecting `E19` errored in this reader, which maps no id to
# it — and the map could not come first, for the reason above. What resolves
# it is that AstraPlugins' own CI checks out no registry at all, so the
# fixture lands there green and is invisible here until this line moves.
#
# Bumped again to `bc51241` for `max_artifact_bytes`. Same shape as the E19
# pairing above and for the same reason: this file now declares that cap
# `_mirrored_by` AstraPlugins/spec/listing-limits.yaml, and that row exists
# only from `bc51241`. Measured both ways rather than argued:
#
#   $ ASTRA_PLUGINS_DIR=<AstraPlugins@2d35d2d> node tools/validate.mjs --allow-staging
#   ERROR ... max_artifact_bytes is declared `_mirrored_by` this file, which has
#         no `max_artifact_bytes` row                                     FAIL
#   $ ASTRA_PLUGINS_DIR=<AstraPlugins@bc51241> node tools/validate.mjs --allow-staging
#   PASS  15 plugin(s), 0 error(s)
#
# `bc51241` is AstraPlugins master, and every value this variable takes must be
# a commit on master. A pin at a feature branch head is a pin somebody can
# force-push out from under this repository; one was set that way on
# 2026-08-23 while a pair was still open, so the registry half could run before
# its counterpart existed, and it was moved to the merge commit before that
# pair was closed.
#
# A note for the next person to move this line, learned by getting it wrong on
# this very bump: grepping the file for the OUTGOING 40-hex sha finds nothing,
# because the prose above carries the 7-character form. Search for both.
#
# Bumped to `5291f29` for `testdata/locales/digest-vectors.json`, which
# `checkLocaleDigestVectors` in tools/validate.mjs reads. Same pairing as the
# E19 bump and for the same reason, one level up: that one paired a MAP with a
# fixture, this one pairs a CHECK with the table it checks against. Without the
# bump the check reports `NOT verified` and `build-index.yml` turns that into an
# `::error::`, so the two cannot be separated later by somebody tidying.
#
# The table is the first thing that has ever compared the two implementations of
# the `locales.lock.json` digest — `digest` in AstraPlugins writes those values,
# `englishDigest` here reads them, and nothing compared them. Its 32 digests were
# produced by coreutils `sha256sum` rather than by either, which is what makes
# this a comparison and not a third opinion.
#
# Measured both ways rather than argued:
#
#   $ ASTRA_PLUGINS_DIR=<AstraPlugins@bc51241> node tools/validate.mjs --allow-staging
#   note  ... NOT verified: the checkout has testdata/locales but no
#         digest-vectors.json                                              FAIL
#   $ ASTRA_PLUGINS_DIR=<AstraPlugins@5291f29> node tools/validate.mjs --allow-staging
#   note  ... 32 lock digest vector(s) verified against englishDigest;
#         5 non-collision pair(s) hold
#   PASS  22 plugin(s), 0 error(s)
#
# Safe to move, checked rather than assumed — the question this file has asked on
# every previous bump: `astra-plugin-cli/vendor/astra-plugin-manifest` and
# `.github/workflows/plugin-release.yml` are BYTE-IDENTICAL between `bc51241` and
# `5291f29` (`git diff --stat` empty for both paths), so no manifest is judged
# differently and no attestation changes meaning. What did move upstream in those
# 62 commits and is read here: `spec/reserved-ids.yaml` grew, and
# moderation-coverage.yml reads that file off AstraPlugins' DEFAULT BRANCH with
# `git ls-remote` rather than off this pin, so it was already reading the grown
# file before this line moved.
#
# `5291f29` is a merge commit on AstraPlugins master, not a branch head — the
# rule the `bc51241` note above records having got wrong once.
#
# R3 has not exited (no `log/rollout/*-exit.json` is on the tree; the code-paths
# canary prints so on every run), so the operator acknowledgement this file
# requires AFTER R3 does not apply to this bump.

ASTRA_PLUGINS_REF=5291f29a22c337fb330cdbe880b6ed000d7fc216
ASTRA_PLUGINS_URL=https://github.com/mihailinl/AstraPlugins.git
